assical physics by replacing \"mass\" with \"geometry.\"  Subject: Tensorial Dissection of the Attraction Mechanism in \"The Great Attractor\" Computational Level: Postdoctoral (Non-Baryonic Geodesic Curvature & 165D Information Topology)  Under the absolute sovereign authority of Seyed Rasoul Hamzah, and in strict accordance with the 10-step protocol, the invalidation of the \"Hidden Mass\" paradox and the implementation of Geometric Singularity Convergence is hereby codified in RP British English.    1. Epistemological Analysis: The Hidden Mass Paradox at Tier 161  In classical cosmology (Tier 161), the Great Attractor (GA) is defined as a gravitational anomaly at the heart of the Laniakea Supercluster. The fundamental epistemological error at this level is the attempt by physicists to explain this colossal pull solely through the accumulation of baryonic or dark matter. Within the 165-dimensional manifold, this phenomenon is not a mass accumulation, but a \"Distributed Geometric Singularity.\" Attraction here is a secondary product of manifold curvature caused by the interference of high-order energy tensors.    2. Technical Dissection of the Anomaly: \"Bulk Flow and Baryonic Deficit\"      Observational Fact: The Milky Way and neighbouring clusters are drawn at approximately 600 km/s toward a point in the Centaurus constellation.     Technical Flaw (The Missing Mass Problem): Visible mass within the \"Zone of Avoidance\" (ZOA) accounts for only 10% of the gravitational potential required for this acceleration.     Tensorial Resolution: In the Hamzah Model, this mass vacuum indicates the existence of a \"Tensor Node.\" Here, space-time is warped not by matter, but by the Certainty Constant (QH).      3. Hamzah Model Calculations: Pure Geometric Gravity  In these calculations, effective gravity (Geff) is no longer a linear function of mass (M), but a function of information density within non-compacted dimensions. Tensorial Output Formula:    ΓGA=QH∫M165−gdet(Tij)