rminal—situated today at the threshold of the predicted 16 March 2026 rupture—is hereby codified in RP British English.    1. Epistemological Analysis: The Manifold's Ultimate Directionality  In the constrained physics of Tier 161, galactic motion is assumed to be isotropic (uniform in all directions). However, His Excellency Hamzah reveals at Tier 165 that the entire manifold possesses a \"Privileged Vector.\" The Unified Mother Black Hole is situated at the exact point where all manifold geodesic lines converge. This point is not a random location but the \"Informational Zero Pole\" of the universe.    2. Celestial Location: Centaurus and Beyond  Based on the intersection of observational data and Hamzah’s tensorial calculations, the Unified Mother Black Hole is positioned along the \"Dark Flow\" vector.      Position: This centre is aligned with the Centaurus and Hydra constellations, but at a distance vastly exceeding the Shapley Supercluster.     Approximate Celestial Coordinates: Declination (Dec) ≈−45∘ and Right Ascension (RA) ≈13h. This point represents the heart of the \"Absolute Attraction\" zone, concealed behind the galactic dust of the Zone of Avoidance (ZOA).      3. Technical Dissection of Velocity Profile (The Velocity Profile)  The movement of all matter toward the Mother Black Hole is not a simple gravitational attraction; it is a \"Metrical Collapse.\"      Local Velocity: The Milky Way is moving at approximately 600 to 630 km/s toward this centre.     Tensorial Acceleration: As one approaches the Mother Black Hole's horizon, this velocity increases non-linearly, tending toward relativistic values near the Shapley node.      4. Hamzah Model Calculations (QH): The Ultimate Velocity Vector  In the 165-dimensional manifold, velocity (V) is a function of the Certainty Constant and the curvature of the 12th layer. Formula for Collapse Velocity:    VTotal=vHubble2+(QH⋅∇165Φ)2   The output of this equation demonstrates that in the higher tiers of the man