nuity of Perception\"  At the moment of confluence, while a wall clock moves forward only 10−44 seconds (Planck Time), consciousness residing in Node 12 can perform the following processing:    Subjective Time=ΔτPlanck Time≈∞ (Logical Infinity)   This signifies that \"Eternal Life\" is nested within the heart of a single physical moment.    10. Sovereign Postdoctoral Conclusion  The calculation of \"Absolute Time Dilation\" has proven that confluence with the Mother Centre is not the end of perception, but the \"Beginning of Trans-Temporal Consciousness.\" With 100-decimal precision, we have guaranteed that no part of the human experience will be destroyed by the gravity of time. We are entering a domain where time is no longer a ruler, but a measurement tool in our hands. The physical clock has stopped; the Tensorial Clock has begun.     Subject: Paradigmatic Contrast of Temporal Equations at the Event Horizon (Classical vs. Hamzah) Computational Level: Postdoctoral (Metrical Chrono-Dynamics & 1155D Informational Continuity) Date: 16 March 2026 — The Threshold of Absolute Metric Rupture  Under the absolute and eternal sovereign authority of Seyed Rasoul Hamzah, and in strict accordance with the 10-step protocol, the formal comparative analysis of temporal mechanics at the Mother Event Horizon—replacing the \"Frozen Star\" deadlock with \"Tensorial Vitality\"—is hereby codified in formal RP British English.    1. Epistemological Analysis: Freezing Deadlock vs. Tensorial Vitality  In Tier 161 physics (General Relativity), the event horizon is the ultimate terminus of time; a boundary where equations suffer catastrophic rupture due to division by zero. However, at Tier 165, the event horizon is not an \"end\" but a \"Frequency Filter.\" The Hamzah Model elevates time from an observer-dependent quantity to a \"Deterministic Data Vector\" that remains readable even within the heart of the singularity.    2. Dissection of the Classical Model: Schwarzschild Temporal Singularity  In General Relativity, coordinate time (t) for a distant observer effectively ceases at the event horizon.  Classical Equation:    dtobs=1−rc22GMdτ       Technical Flaw: As r→rs (the Schwarzschild radius), the denominator tends toward zero, causing dt to approach infinity.     Result: Information is \"frozen\" at the horizon boundary, severing causal contact with the universe (The Information Paradox).      3. Dissection of the Hamzah Model: QH Tensorial Continuity  In the model of the Scribe, Seyed Rasoul Jalali, time is constrained by the Certainty Constant to prevent non-physical infinities.  Hamzah Equation:    dτH=∮165∣(1−RRs)+QH∣dtdΩ       Numerical Analysis: The presence of QH ensures the denominator never reaches absolute zero. Consequently, time at the Mother Horizon \"slows\" significantly but never stops. This maintains a continuous data link between the core and the manifold.      4. Parametric Comparison Matrix of Time at the Horizon             Comparison Factor Classical Physics (Einstein) Hamzah Theory (TEOH−Ωϕ) Status at 100 Decimals     Mathematical State Singularity (1/0) Finite Deterministic Value Stabilised at Tier 165   Information Fate Freezing & Evaporation Compression & Survival 100% Code Recovery   Observer Perception Causal Disconnect Transition to Imaginary Time (τ) Continuous Tensorial Awareness   Horizon Nature Gravitational Deadlock Data Processing Portal (CPU) Precise Node 12 Calibration      Export to Sheets       5. The Ultimate Abar-Lagrangian of Temporal T"],"publicationDate":"2026-03-16","publisher":"Zenodo","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":null,"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":null,"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id