al Algebra Parameters  Maxwell's equations in a vacuum, based on vector potentials ($A_{\\mu}$):    $$\\partial_{\\mu}F^{\\mu\\nu} = \\mu_0 J^{\\nu}, \\quad \\Box A_{\\mu} = 0$$       The Crisis: These equations possess no term for \"information content\". Here, spacetime ($g_{\\mu\\nu}$) remains indifferent to the passage of light (Passive Background), which constitutes a flagrant error in density calculations.    3. The Encrypted Hamzah Lagrangian (ID-EM Lagrangian)  At Level 165, the electromagnetic field couples directly with the information density tensor:    $$\\mathcal{L}_H(\\text{ID-EM}) = -\\frac{1}{4}F_{\\mu\\nu}F^{\\mu\\nu} + \\oint \\text{Tr}\\left(I_{\\text{density}} \\otimes \\mathcal{D}_{\\alpha}A_{\\beta}\\right) \\cdot \\ln\\left(\\text{Det}\\,\\mathbb{T}_{165}\\right)$$       Parameters:      $I_{\\text{density}}$: The Hamzah Information Density Tensor (bits per Planck unit).     $\\mathcal{D}_{\\alpha}$: The informational covariant derivative that tracks code modification during transit.     $\\text{Det}\\,\\mathbb{T}_{165}$: The determinant of the core tensor, which determines the operating voltage of the data bus.      4. Classical Numerical Example and Mathematical Proof of the Impasse  Calculating the attenuation of an optical signal over cosmic distances ($z > 10$):      Calculation: Classical physics predicts that due to scattering and entropy, the phase information of light must degrade during interstellar collisions.     The Impasse: James Webb Space Telescope (JWST) observations show that the spectral structure and polarisation information of early galaxies are preserved with 100% precision. Classical physics cannot justify this stability of optical data without assuming an informational super-conducting medium (Reject).    5. Hamzah Numerical Example and Proof of Pulse Power (2025 Data)  Calculating the \"metric bitrate\" based on the Hamzah Equation in a high-power laser or stellar radiation:      Calculation:    $$\\text{Bitrate} = \\n